 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition of\nI. Adieu! Some Maidens have departed\nLike stars; but all are fair to me again.\nWith whom ye mourned? 'Tis not the only.\nII. E'en her who first met me on our\nFirst visit for joy - or with a sorrow.\nIII. In many a hour we parted.\nThe heart grew thine, the flower is ours.\nIV. How in words could I sooth our\nLove's last sorrows as it came upon.\nV. O sweet friend of old love, of many!\nSweet hearts and loving lips are ours.",
